    "contentHtml": "<h1>Toxic &amp; Safe Foods for Dogs</h1>\n<p>Ingested into Pinecone as a 20-pair Q&amp;A pack on 2026-06-30. Source: <code>qa-toxic-and-safe-foods.json</code>.\nGrounded in veterinary toxicology (ASPCA APCC, Pet Poison Helpline, NIH/PMC). Part of [[Nutrition]].</p>\n<h2>Emergency numbers</h2>\n<p>ASPCA Animal Poison Control: <strong>(888) 426-4435</strong> · Pet Poison Helpline: <strong>(855) 764-7661</strong>.\nAct fast, don&#39;t wait for symptoms; don&#39;t induce vomiting unless told to.</p>\n<h2>TOXIC — with actual thresholds/mechanisms</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Xylitol</strong> (sweetener; hidden in gum, some peanut butter) — insulin dump → hypoglycemia ~<strong>0.1 g/kg</strong>, liver failure ~<strong>0.5 g/kg</strong>. Most dangerous common toxin.</li>\n<li><strong>Chocolate</strong> — theobromine + caffeine. Signs ~<strong>20 mg/kg</strong>, cardiac ~40–50, seizures ~60 mg/kg. Darker = worse; white ≈ none.</li>\n<li><strong>Grapes/raisins</strong> — <strong>tartaric acid</strong> (current leading theory) → acute kidney failure. <strong>No safe dose</strong> (idiosyncratic). Raisins more concentrated.</li>\n<li><strong>Onions</strong> (+ leeks/shallots/chives) — thiosulfates → Heinz-body hemolytic anemia ~<strong>5 g/kg</strong>; <strong>cumulative</strong>; cooked/powder worse. Delayed signs.</li>\n<li><strong>Garlic</strong> — same allium mechanism, ~5x more potent than onion; toxic studies used ~5 g/kg. <strong>BUT</strong> holistic dose (~1/4 clove per 10 lb) is far below toxic — dose-dependent, safe in moderation for dogs, <strong>never cats</strong>. (Honest reconciliation with our [[Holistic Parasite Prevention and Natural Deworming]] garlic guidance.)</li>\n<li><strong>Macadamia nuts</strong> — toxic ~<strong>2 g/kg</strong>; weakness/tremors/hyperthermia; usually recover 24–48h.</li>\n<li><strong>Alcohol &amp; raw yeast dough</strong> — ethanol; dough also rises → bloat. Emergency.</li>\n<li><strong>Caffeine/coffee</strong> — stimulant like theobromine; grounds/beans concentrated.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Often OVERSTATED / nuance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Avocado</strong> — persin toxic to birds, dogs fairly resistant; flesh in small amounts ok; real risks = pit (obstruction) + fat.</li>\n<li><strong>Cooked bones / corn cobs / pits</strong> — physical hazards (splinter / obstruction), not poisons.</li>\n<li><strong>Dairy</strong> — lactose upset varies; plain yogurt/kefir usually fine + probiotic.</li>\n<li><strong>Fatty/salty foods</strong> — pancreatitis (fat), sodium issues (salt). Not &quot;toxic&quot; but real harm.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>SAFE &amp; healthy (the fun list)</h2>\n<p>Blueberries (antioxidants), carrots, plain pumpkin (fiber), eggs (protein), plain yogurt/kefir (probiotics),\nsardines (omega-3), apples (no seeds), green beans, sweet potato, watermelon (no seeds/rind), cucumber,\nxylitol-free peanut butter. Rule: ~10% of calories, one new thing at a time, plain (no salt/sugar/onion/garlic).</p>\n"
