    "contentHtml": "<h1>Zoonotic Parasites (dog → human)</h1>\n<p>9-pair pack ingested 2026-07-04 under [[PINECONE_PROTOCOL]]. Sourced to CDC/CAPC. The <em>accurate, sensible-hygiene</em>\ncounter to the alarmist &quot;never let your dog inside / don&#39;t kiss your dog&quot; human-cleanse framing we rejected. Related [[Holistic Parasite Prevention and Natural Deworming]].</p>\n<h2>The real zoonotic risks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🟡 <strong>Roundworm (Toxocara canis)</strong> — biggest concern; causes visceral/ocular larva migrans. Eggs pass in stool but need days–weeks in soil to become infective → kids ingest matured eggs (pica). CDC: 1–3M larva-migrans cases/yr.</li>\n<li>🟡 <strong>Hookworm (Ancylostoma)</strong> — larvae penetrate skin (bare feet on contaminated soil/sand) → cutaneous larva migrans (itchy tracks).</li>\n<li>🟡 <strong>Flea tapeworm (Dipylidium)</strong> — rare, mostly kids swallowing an infected flea. Echinococcus = serious but regional.</li>\n<li>🟡 <strong>Giardia — MYTH-CORRECTION:</strong> most canine strains are NOT readily transmitted to humans; pets aren&#39;t the source of most human Giardia.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who&#39;s at risk / prevention</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Highest risk: <strong>young children</strong> (pica, hand-to-mouth, sandboxes), immunocompromised, pregnant. Healthy adults = low risk.</li>\n<li>🟢 <strong>Prevention (handles nearly all of it):</strong> prompt stool pickup (before eggs mature), hand-washing, routine deworming/prevention + stool checks, deworm puppies early, shoes outside, cover sandboxes, don&#39;t let kids eat dirt.</li>\n<li>🟡 <strong>You do NOT need to banish the dog / stop cuddling</strong> — transmission is via contaminated SOIL, not casual contact with a dewormed dog. Reasonable hygiene, not paranoia.</li>\n<li>Puppies = highest shedders (born with/acquire worms via placenta/milk) → early vet deworming schedule.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<p>CDC — Toxocariasis / cutaneous larva migrans; CAPC puppy deworming + zoonosis; Today&#39;s Veterinary Nurse 2024 &quot;Limiting Zoonotic Risks of Internal Parasites&quot;; dvm360 parasitic zoonoses.</p>\n"
